  "fullDescription": "Procreate Brush #39 – Abstract Suite – INSTANT DIGITAL DOWNLOAD – 1 Procreate Brush – Requires Procreate app + iPad / iPad Pro / iPhone\n\nA unique quirky abstract Procreate digital brush created from an illustration I digitally hand drew. Inspired by an Art Deco, art nouveau, dark academia, Steampunk, elegant, fancy, mystical, fantasy, mood. A brush for versatile drawing, painting, doodling, sketching, jewelry / jewellery, necklace, bracelet, lace, clothing, tattoo, outfit embellishments, spider web, curly branch, tree aesthetic, witch, witchy, magic, magical, fairy, luxury, classy lines, decoration, line art, paint borders, ornaments, fabric, symmetry, symmetrical, geometric patterns, stamp, bold graphic design, shapes, abstract lines, ink pen doodles, shapes, cartoons, comics, anime, manga, retro vintage Summer, Spring, Fall, Autumn, Winter fashion, clothes, clothing accessories, fabric, stitching, sewing embellishments, outfits, garments, architecture, house decor, interior decoration elements, iPad / iPad Pro hand lettering, portrait art, makeup, nail art, earrings, accessories, illustrating for holidays, parties & celebrations like Halloween, Thanksgiving, Christmas, Xmas, New Year, Easter, Valentines Day, Birthday Parties, Baby Showers, work office parties, school, homeschool, events, work schedules, school, college, university graduation card decor, Weddings, Thanksgiving, Halloween, casual get together stationary and more, an intricate, cute, kawaii, boho, fancy, elegant, classy aesthetic brush you can use for many other types of projects too such as painting, illustrating, sketching, drawing, scrapbooking, scrapbook doodles, borders, picture frames, planning, organising, crafts, and more.\n\nHappy drawing 🙂\n\nWHAT’S INCLUDED:\n-1 Procreate digital brush\n\nMORE INFO ON THE BRUSH:\nBrush #39 – 1 individual Procreate brush from the ‘Abstract Suite Collection’ series of Procreate Brushes in this shop (ZaraRozaDesigns)\n\n-This brush has pressure sensitive size. Pressing harder and the width of the line will get bigger, press lighter and the line width will get narrower.\n\nIMPORTING THE BRUSH TO PROCREATE:\n\n-Go to downloads on your ipad or the location you downloaded the .brush file to.\n\n-Press on the .brush file, then it should import to Procreate (the iPad should automatically take you to Procreate, say ‘importing’ with a blue tick under it).\n\n-Click on any artwork or create a new artwork. Then go to the brush icon in Procreate (on the upper right) and the ‘Brush Library’ dropdown menu should appear. Scroll up through the list of brush sets on the left to the top where the brush set should be.\n\nThank you so much for stopping by the shop. Happy drawing! 🙂\n\nZara Roza Designs",
